      "index": 17,
      "refined_text": "The current p95 is 420 milliseconds and p99 is 1.8 seconds. We should not optimize only for p95 because the tail latency is where the customer-visible timeouts happen.",
      "changes": []
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "refined_text": "There is another issue with retries. The gateway uses exponential backoff with a maximum of 30 seconds, while our Kafka consumer retry policy currently allows 5 attempts.",
      "changes": []
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "refined_text": "If the gateway times out after sending the authorization request, we cannot assume the authorization failed. The next retry has to query the provider or use the idempotency key.",
